        "description": "Company values are supposed to make decisions clearer. But in most businesses, they stay vague enough that every manager interprets them differently.\n\nIn this video, we turn one common value, Ownership, into a practical operating behavior your team can use when a deadline slips, a customer is unhappy, or nobody is sure who should act.\n\n*You’ll see how to:*\n- Turn a vague company value into a clear decision rule\n- Define what the value looks like in real work\n- Create a three-level Values Practice Guide\n- Use values in hiring, onboarding, debriefs, recognition, and team moments\n- Let AI organize examples and draft useful questions without letting it judge people\n\n*JOIN OUR CIRCLE COMMUNITY FOR FREE*\nhttps://community.empowerlabs.ai/join?invitation_token=f618616a09ca533f4c5457fb0f922e7935adc13e-93fdb8d8-0742-437f-a65e-c24b9174bb85\n\n*Robert Glazer’s AI Core Values Coach:* https://robertglazer.com/gpt\n\n*Chapters:*\n0:00 When values don’t help decisions\n0:33 Why values usually fail\n1:07 Turn a vague value into behavior\n2:15 Define ownership with a real example\n2:58 Build a three-level practice guide\n3:18 Use values in team moments\n3:59 Use AI to organize values examples\n4:41 One value to clarify this week\n\n#AIForBusiness #CompanyValues #OperatingSystems",
